cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code, cite it as below."
title: "YvO_2026: skeletal muscle proteome response to resistance training in younger and older adults"
type: software
version: "2.1"
authors:
  - family-names: Lewis
    given-names: Dustyn
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0000-9558-275X"
license: MIT
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.19886624
repository-code: "https://github.com/Dustyn-T-Lewis/YvO_2026"
abstract: >-
  Analysis code for a study of the vastus lateralis proteome in younger and
  older adults before and after resistance training. Thirty-two participants
  gave a biopsy before and after training, 64 samples in all, quantified by
  DIA mass spectrometry. Two outlier samples, Y_S05_Pre and Y_S07_Post, are
  removed, leaving 2,106 proteins across 62 samples. limma tests four
  contrasts: aging, training in younger adults, training in older adults, and
  the age by training interaction. The code runs from the raw intensity
  workbook to every figure and supplementary table of the revised manuscript.
keywords:
  - proteomics
  - skeletal muscle
  - resistance training
  - aging
  - limma
  - WGCNA
